@startuml
title Proposed Phase 6 — reliable deletion and notification flow
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

participant "Post Service" as Post
database "Post DB + Outbox" as PostDB
participant "Comment Service" as Comment
database "Comment DB + Outbox" as CommentDB
participant "Interaction Service" as Interaction
database "Interaction DB + Outbox" as InteractionDB
queue Kafka
participant "Notification Service" as Notification
database "Notification DB\nprocessed_event IDs" as NotificationDB

note over Post,Notification
  PROPOSED — implement only after CR contracts are ACCEPTED.
  Every event has UUID eventId, version, occurredAt UTC and correlationId.
end note

== Business command plus outbox ==
Comment -> CommentDB : transaction: save comment + outbox event
CommentDB --> Comment : commit succeeds without depending on Kafka
Comment -> Kafka : relay CommentCreatedV1 / CommentRepliedV1

Interaction -> InteractionDB : transaction: ledger/counter + outbox event
InteractionDB --> Interaction : commit
Interaction -> Kafka : relay ReactionCreatedV1 / ReactionRemovedV1

== Idempotent notification ==
Kafka -> Notification : event (may be delivered more than once)
Notification -> NotificationDB : INSERT eventId if absent
alt First delivery and actor != recipient
  Notification -> NotificationDB : create notification in same transaction
else Duplicate or self-action
  Notification -> NotificationDB : no duplicate notification
end

== Cross-service deletion policy ==
Post -> PostDB : transaction: delete/visibility change + PostDeletedV1 outbox
Post -> Kafka : relay PostDeletedV1
Kafka -> Comment : idempotently archive/hide per accepted policy
Comment -> CommentDB : local policy update + optional CommentDeletedV1 outbox
Kafka -> Interaction : idempotently remove/tombstone POST reactions
Interaction -> InteractionDB : reconcile ledger and counters

Comment -> CommentDB : soft-delete comment + CommentDeletedV1 outbox
Comment -> Kafka : relay CommentDeletedV1
Kafka -> Interaction : idempotently remove/tombstone COMMENT reactions
Interaction -> InteractionDB : reconcile ledger and counters

... transient consumer failure ...
Kafka -> Notification : bounded retry topic
Kafka -> Notification : DLT / parking lot after retry exhaustion
@enduml
